      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(-x^{5}-4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-x^{5}-4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(-x^{5}-4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -\\int x^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-4\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -\\frac{x^{5+1}}{(5+1)}-4\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{x^{6}}{6}-4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
