      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(-4+x^{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-4+x^{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(-4+x^{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -4\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -4\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{x^{5+1}}{(5+1)}+C \\\\ &= -4x+\\frac{x^{6}}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
